  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved food and livelihood security in Bangladesh (Action on Disability and Development)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of a programme in which four Bangladeshi partners are collaborating together in order to address food and livelihood insecurity, which were identified as the key problems in Bagerhat district.  The partners hold regular meetings and build up linkages with other networks through which monitoring information, reviews, evaluations and experiences can be shared.  Action on Disability and Development (ADD) is taking the lead role in advocating for people with disabilities to be fully included in all development, disaster preparedness, reduction and response work as well as advocating livelihoods security of vulnerable people in the context of the climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
